name			wine11
version		11.20-85
architecture	x86_64
summary		"Run Windows programs on Haiku and RenkuOS (Wine 11.20, experimental)"
description		"Wine 11.20 with a Haiku port, for running Windows programs on 64-bit Haiku and RenkuOS. This is an
experimental port: some programs do not work, and programs that use the graphics card have hung or frozen the whole
system. It is offered as it is.

What works: 64-bit programs, windows and menus, tray icons (in the Deskbar), sound playing and recording, MIDI,
OpenGL, and Direct3D through DXVK.

Before the first use, run `wineboot -u` and then `wineserver -w` to make a prefix. Programs open with a double-click
through Wine Launcher.

Not in this package:
- 32-bit programs (many games and installers, Steam among them) need the wine_compat kernel add-on, which depends on
the kernel version. Install it before making the prefix. Without it only 64-bit programs run.
- Some programs (Chromium, WebView2, the Firefox sandbox) also need the wine_int3 kernel add-on.
- Graphics card support needs an NVIDIA card and the Nebula driver package. Direct3D games also need DXVK in the
prefix.

Downloads, instructions and release notes: https://github.com/ablyssx74/wine/releases"
packager		"ablyssx74 <ablyssx74@users.noreply.github.com>"
vendor			ablyssx74
copyrights		{ "1993-2026 the Wine project authors" "2026 ablyssx74" }
licenses		{ "GNU LGPL v2.1" }
urls			{ "https://github.com/ablyssx74/wine" }
provides		{
	wine11 = 11.20
	cmd:wine11 = 11.20
}
requires		{
	haiku >= r1~beta6
	wayland
	libxkbcommon
	gnutls
	mimalloc
}
